1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
OFFICER: Good morning. What can I do for you?

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
LOUISE: I want to report a theft. I had some things stolen out of my bag yesterday.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,660
OFFICER: I'm sorry to hear that. Right, so I'll need to take a few details

4
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:20,170
Can I start with your name?

5
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:22,620
LOUISE: Louise Taylor.

6
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:27,510
OFFICER: OK, thank you. And are you resident in the UK?

7
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:32,580
LOUISE: No, I'm actually Canadian, though my mother was British.

8
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,060
OFFICER: And your date of birth?

9
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:39,480
LOUISE: December 14th, 1977.

10
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,000
OFFICER: So you're just visiting this country?

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,084
LOUISE: That's right. I come over most summers on business.

12
00:00:47,084 --> 00:00:53,210
I'm an interior designer and I come over to buy old furniture, antiques you know.

13
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:56,100
There are some really lovely things around here

14
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:59,237
but you need to get out to the small towns.

15
00:00:59,237 --> 00:01:02,920
I've had a really good trip this year, until this happened.

16
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:07,000
OFFICER: OK. So you've been here quite a while?

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,210
LOUISE: Yes, I'm here for two months. I go back next week.

18
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:15,840
OFFICER: So may I ask where you're staying now?

19
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:22,500
LOUISE: Well at present I've got a place at Park Apartments, that's on King Street.

20
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,625
I was staying at the Riverside Apartments on the same street,

21
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:30,160
but the apartment there was only available for six weeks

22
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:33,000
so I had to find another one.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,470
OFFICER: OK. And the apartment number?

24
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:38,570
LOUISE: Fifteen.

25
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:40,220
OFFICER: Right.

26
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:44,510
OFFICER: Now, I need to take some details of the theft.

27
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:49,190
So you said you had some things stolen out of your bag?

28
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:51,120
LOUISE: That's right.

29
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:56,660
OFFICER: And were you actually carrying the bag when the theft took place?

30
00:01:56,660 --> 00:02:01,280
Yes. I really can't understand it. I had my backpack on.

31
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:05,620
And I went into a supermarket to buy a few things

32
00:02:06,303 --> 00:02:10,100
and when I opened it up my wallet wasn't there

33
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:14,000
OFFICER: And what did your wallet have in it?

34
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,882
LOUISE: Well, fortunately I don't keep my credit cards in that wallet -

35
00:02:18,882 --> 00:02:24,170
I keep them with my passport in an inside compartment in my backpack.

36
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:32,170
But there was quite a bit of cash there... about £250 sterling, I should think.

37
00:02:32,170 --> 00:02:35,422
I withdrew £300 from my account yesterday,

38
00:02:35,422 --> 00:02:43,320
but I did a bit of shopping, so I must have already spent about £50 of that.

39
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:45,170
OFFICER: OK.

40
00:02:45,170 --> 00:02:46,989
LOUISE: At first I thought,

41
00:02:46,989 --> 00:02:50,340
oh I must have left the wallet back in the apartment

42
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:54,630
but then I realised my phone had gone as well.

43
00:02:54,630 --> 00:03:00,144
It was only a week old, and that's when I realised I'd been robbed.

44
00:03:00,144 --> 00:03:04,870
Anyway at least they didn't take the keys to my rental car.

45
00:03:04,870 --> 00:03:10,210
OFFICER: Yes. So you say the theft occurred yesterday?

46
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:12,000
LOUISE: Yes.

47
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,007
OFFICER: So that was September the tenth.

48
00:03:15,007 --> 00:03:19,360
And do you have any idea at all of where or

49
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:23,170
when the things might possibly have been stolen?

50
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:26,107
LOUISE: Well at first I couldn't believe it

51
00:03:26,107 --> 00:03:31,980
because the bag had been on my back ever since I left the apartment after lunch.

52
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:34,420
It's just a small backpack

53
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:40,066
but I generally use it when I'm travelling because it seems safer than a handbag.

54
00:03:40,066 --> 00:03:46,940
Anyway, I met up with a friend, and we spent a couple of hours in the museum.

55
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:50,727
But I do remember that as we were leaving there,

56
00:03:50,727 --> 00:03:55,360
at about 4 o'clock, a group of young boys ran up to us

57
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:58,302
and they were really crowding round us,

58
00:03:58,302 --> 00:04:04,740
and they were asking us what time it was, then all of a sudden they ran off.

59
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:08,440
OFFICER: Can you remember anything about them?

60
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:15,271
LOUISE: The one who did most of the talking was wearing a T-shirt

61
00:04:15,271 --> 00:04:20,000
with a picture of something... let's see... a tiger.

62
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,380
OFFICER: Right. Any idea of how old he might have been?

63
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:27,880
LOUISE: Around twelve years old?

64
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:32,740
OFFICER: And can you remember anything else about his appearance?

65
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:37,610
LOUISE: Not much. He was quite thin...

66
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:39,760
OFFICER: Colour of hair?

67
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:46,330
LOUISE: I do remember that - he was blond. All the others were dark-haired.

68
00:04:46,330 --> 00:04:49,900
OFFICER: And any details of the others?

69
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:55,130
LOUISE: Not really. They came and went so quickly.

70
00:04:55,130 --> 00:05:02,309
OFFICER: Right. So what I'm going to do now is give you a crime reference number

71
00:05:02,309 --> 00:05:05,450
so you can contact your insurance company.

72
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:11,900
So this is ten digits: 87954

73
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:15,080
82361

74
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:17,720
LOUISE: Thank you.
